// The panel's decision (Fed. Cir. IOP #8-#9; Fed. Cir. R. 36), the remand
// router, and rehearing (Fed. Cir. R. 40), whose 30-day period is the
// Federal Circuit's local extension of FRAP 40(d)(1)'s 14 days.
module cafc.decision-to-rehearing

import cafc.mandate.{ mandate-issued }
import cafc.{ BecameFinal, Entered, Filed, Order, Paper, decision-group, rehearing-group }
import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frap26.{ frap26 }

/// A tribunal-discretion draw. It stays a `decision` by `office`, as in the
/// pack, because a `chance` node lowers to kind `state`; its probabilities
/// are the pack's, with their bases in each edge's note.
chance panel-decision: "Panel Decides the Appeal" by office discretion cite "Fed. Cir. IOP #8; Fed. Cir. IOP #9; FRAP 36"
{
  group decision-group
  note "Straw vote in reverse seniority order on outcome and disposition vehicle (precedential opinion, nonprecedential opinion, or Rule 36 judgment) — IOP #8 ¶ 1; IOP #9 ¶ 1. Probability basis: the Federal Circuit issued Rule 36 summary affirmances in ~20% of merits terminations in 2024 (Jason Rantanen, 'Federal Circuit Decisions - 2024 Stats and Datapack,' Patently-O, June 2025) — the only figure on this node's edges independently sourced to a cited statistic; note the same source finds the Rule 36 rate is far higher in PTAB-origin appeals specifically (43% of PTAB appeals 2011-2024, and 67% vs 18% depending on whether the patent owner or the petitioner is the appellant) — not separately modeled here since this pack does not branch panel-decision by origin. The remaining five splits (opinion-affirmed, reversed outright, vacated/remanded, mixed, dismissed) apportion the balance as teaching estimates and are NOT independently sourced — flagged APPROXIMATE, consistent with ptab-patent-trial-appeal-board.json's and itc-337.json's own convention for unsourced splits."
  panel-to-rule36 "Panel enters a Rule 36 judgment of affirmance without opinion" -> rule36-affirmance p 0.2 {
    authority cite "Fed. Cir. R. 36(a)"
    note "~20% of 2024 merits terminations per patentlyo-2024-datapack. Sets panel-affirmed so cert-not-sought/cert-denied can restore this outcome's payoff if rehearing/cert is entered and denied — see docs/PACK_SCHEMA.md#state-flags and docs/CRITIQUE.md."
    sets [panel-affirmed]
  }
  panel-to-affirmed "Panel affirms with an opinion" -> affirmed p 0.28 {
    authority cite "FRAP 36(a)"
    note "Teaching estimate apportioning the non-Rule-36 balance — not independently sourced."
    sets [panel-affirmed]
  }
  panel-to-reversed "Panel reverses outright, no remand" -> reversed p 0.1 {
    authority cite "FRAP 36(a)"
    note "Teaching estimate — not independently sourced."
    sets [panel-reversed]
  }
  panel-to-remand "Panel vacates and remands" -> remand-destination p 0.2 {
    authority cite "FRAP 36(a)"
    note "Teaching estimate — not independently sourced."
  }
  panel-to-mixed "Panel splits the result" -> affirmed-in-part-reversed-in-part p 0.17 {
    authority cite "FRAP 36(a)"
    note "Teaching estimate — not independently sourced."
    sets [panel-mixed]
  }
  panel-to-dismissed "Panel dismisses for a jurisdictional/mootness defect" -> dismissed-jurisdictional-defect p 0.05 {
    authority cite "28 U.S.C. § 1295; FRAP 3"
    note "Teaching estimate — not independently sourced."
  }
}

terminal rule36-affirmance: "Rule 36 Judgment of Affirmance Without Opinion" by applicant outcome [loss] cite "Fed. Cir. R. 36(a)-(b)"
{
  group decision-group
  note "Entered when an opinion would have no precedential value and one of Rule 36(a)(1)-(5) applies (findings not clearly erroneous; sufficient evidence for a jury verdict; record supports SJ/directed verdict/JOP; agency decision warrants affirmance under its governing standard of review; or no error of law). No separate judgment is prepared — the order is the judgment (Fed. Cir. R. 36(b)). Payoff 0 per the authoring brief's convention (affirmed-for-appellee)."
  valence bad
  payoff 0.usd
  rule36-to-rehearing "Losing party weighs rehearing" -> rehearing-window {
    authority cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(a)(1)"
  }
}

terminal affirmed: "Affirmed (With Opinion)" by applicant outcome [loss] cite "FRAP 36(a)"
{
  group decision-group
  valence bad
  payoff 0.usd
  affirmed-to-rehearing "Losing party weighs rehearing" -> rehearing-window {
    authority cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(a)(1)"
  }
}

terminal reversed: "Reversed (No Remand)" by applicant outcome [win] cite "FRAP 36(a)"
{
  group decision-group
  note "Relatively rare outright disposition — most reversals on questions requiring further fact-finding or application of law route through vacatur-and-remand instead."
  valence good
  payoff 1_000_000.usd
  reversed-to-rehearing "Losing party weighs rehearing" -> rehearing-window {
    authority cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(a)(1)"
  }
}

terminal affirmed-in-part-reversed-in-part: "Affirmed in Part, Reversed in Part" by applicant outcome [remand] cite "FRAP 36(a)"
{
  group decision-group
  note "Illustrative mixed-result payoff (between the 0 affirmance and 1,000,000 reversal anchors); in practice a mixed disposition often carries its own remand on the reversed portion, not separately modeled as a route into the remand-destination node to keep the graph tractable."
  valence caution
  tags [mixed]
  payoff 250_000.usd
  mixed-to-rehearing "Either party weighs rehearing" -> rehearing-window {
    authority cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(a)(1)"
  }
}

terminal dismissed-jurisdictional-defect: "Dismissed — Jurisdictional/Mootness Defect Found on Appeal" outcome [procedural-default] cite "28 U.S.C. § 1295; FRAP 3"
{
  group decision-group
  note "E.g., prematurity, mootness, or a defect in the judgment appealed from discovered at the merits stage rather than screened out earlier."
  valence bad
  payoff 0.usd
}

/// Where a vacated judgment goes back to is a matter fact (`tags [fact]`),
/// not a draw: the tribunal the appeal came from, which the matter's
/// history names by the entry that opened its notice-of-appeal period
/// (`Entered(Judgment)` a district court's, `Entered(CofcJudgment)` the
/// Court of Federal Claims', `Entered(BoardDecision)` the PTAB's,
/// `Entered(TtabDecision)` the TTAB's, `BecameFinal()` the ITC's). Each
/// guard holds only when that one origin's entry is in the history, so
/// they are disjoint, and a history naming none (or several) decides
/// nothing: the matter states its `facts`. The probabilities are only the
/// prior of a matter whose history does not decide it; each `cafc@origin`
/// instance sets its own route to 1.
chance remand-destination: "Vacated/Remanded — Destination Tribunal" by office cite "FRAP 36(a)"
{
  group decision-group
  note "A matter fact, not an independent statistical draw: which of the remand terminals applies is determined entirely by the tribunal the appeal came from, which replay reads from the matter's own entry event. The 0.25/0.25/0.25/0.25 split is only the prior of a matter whose history does not name its origin -- see cafc-SOURCES-NOTES.md."
  tags [fact]
  remand-route-district-court "Case originated at the district court" -> remanded-to-district-court p 0.25 {
    when has_event(Entered(Judgment)) && !has_event(Entered(CofcJudgment)) && !has_event(Entered(BoardDecision)) && !has_event(Entered(TtabDecision)) && !has_event(BecameFinal())
    authority cite "FRAP 36(a)"
    note "Prior only -- see remand-destination's note."
  }
  remand-route-ptab "Case originated at the PTAB" -> remanded-to-ptab p 0.25 {
    when has_event(Entered(BoardDecision)) && !has_event(Entered(Judgment)) && !has_event(Entered(CofcJudgment)) && !has_event(Entered(TtabDecision)) && !has_event(BecameFinal())
    authority cite "FRAP 36(a)"
    note "Prior only -- see remand-destination's note."
  }
  remand-route-itc "Case originated at the ITC" -> remanded-to-itc p 0.25 {
    when has_event(BecameFinal()) && !has_event(Entered(Judgment)) && !has_event(Entered(CofcJudgment)) && !has_event(Entered(BoardDecision)) && !has_event(Entered(TtabDecision))
    authority cite "FRAP 36(a)"
    note "Prior only -- see remand-destination's note."
  }
  remand-route-cofc "Case originated at the CoFC" -> remanded-to-cofc p 0.25 {
    when has_event(Entered(CofcJudgment)) && !has_event(Entered(Judgment)) && !has_event(Entered(BoardDecision)) && !has_event(Entered(TtabDecision)) && !has_event(BecameFinal())
    authority cite "FRAP 36(a)"
    note "Prior only -- see remand-destination's note."
  }
  remand-route-ttab "Case originated at the TTAB" -> remanded-to-ttab p 0 {
    when has_event(Entered(TtabDecision)) && !has_event(Entered(Judgment)) && !has_event(Entered(CofcJudgment)) && !has_event(Entered(BoardDecision)) && !has_event(BecameFinal())
    authority cite "FRAP 36(a)"
    note "Prior only -- see remand-destination's note. Authored 0.0 in the unscoped base so the existing four 0.25 splits (and every base-pack output) are unchanged; the cafc@ttab instance sets this route to 1.0."
  }
}

terminal remanded-to-district-court: "Remanded to the District Court" outcome [remand] {
  group decision-group
  note "Illustrative payoff per the authoring brief (~40% of the full-reversal value — a real but incomplete win; the case is not over). This terminal's id is deliberately stable so packs/links.json composition can link it back into the corresponding origin pack's post-remand posture (e.g. mpep-prosecution.json for PTAB, itc-337.json's commission-final-determination for a remand, frcp-civil-procedure.json for district court)."
  valence caution
  payoff 400_000.usd
}

terminal remanded-to-ptab: "Remanded to the PTAB" outcome [remand] {
  group decision-group
  note "Illustrative payoff per the authoring brief (~40% of the full-reversal value — a real but incomplete win; the case is not over). This terminal's id is deliberately stable so packs/links.json composition can link it back into the corresponding origin pack's post-remand posture (e.g. mpep-prosecution.json for PTAB, itc-337.json's commission-final-determination for a remand, frcp-civil-procedure.json for district court)."
  valence caution
  payoff 400_000.usd
}

terminal remanded-to-itc: "Remanded to the ITC" outcome [remand] {
  group decision-group
  note "Illustrative payoff per the authoring brief (~40% of the full-reversal value — a real but incomplete win; the case is not over). This terminal's id is deliberately stable so packs/links.json composition can link it back into the corresponding origin pack's post-remand posture (e.g. mpep-prosecution.json for PTAB, itc-337.json's commission-final-determination for a remand, frcp-civil-procedure.json for district court)."
  valence caution
  payoff 400_000.usd
}

terminal remanded-to-cofc: "Remanded to the Court of Federal Claims" outcome [remand] {
  group decision-group
  note "Illustrative payoff per the authoring brief (~40% of the full-reversal value — a real but incomplete win; the case is not over). This terminal's id is deliberately stable so packs/links.json composition can link it back into the corresponding origin pack's post-remand posture (e.g. mpep-prosecution.json for PTAB, itc-337.json's commission-final-determination for a remand, frcp-civil-procedure.json for district court)."
  valence caution
  payoff 400_000.usd
}

terminal remanded-to-ttab: "Remanded to the TTAB" outcome [remand] {
  group decision-group
  note "Illustrative payoff per the authoring brief (~40% of the full-reversal value — a real but incomplete win; the case is not over). This terminal's id is deliberately stable so packs/links.json composition can link it back into the corresponding origin pack's post-remand posture (e.g. mpep-prosecution.json for TTAB, itc-337.json's commission-final-determination for a remand, frcp-civil-procedure.json for district court)."
  valence caution
  payoff 400_000.usd
}

decision rehearing-window: "Losing Party Weighs Rehearing" by applicant cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(a)(1), (f)"
{
  group rehearing-group
  rehearing-file "File petition for panel rehearing/rehearing en banc/combined petition" -> rehearing-petition-filed {
    authority cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(a)-(b), (f)"
    effort 90.hours
    cost 0.usd
    event Filed(RehearingPetition)
    within rehearing-period {
      extendable false
      note "30 days after entry of judgment on the panel decision; 45 days if the United States or its officer/agency is a party (Fed. Cir. R. 40(f)(1))."
    }
    tags [appeal]
  }
  rehearing-time-expires "No rehearing sought — time expires" -> mandate-issued {
    authority cite "FRAP 41(b); Fed. Cir. R. 41"
    within rehearing-period {
      note "If no petition is timely filed (30/45 days), the mandate issues 7 days after that period expires."
    }
  }
}

state rehearing-petition-filed: "Petition for Panel Rehearing / Rehearing En Banc / Combined Petition Filed" by office cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(a)(1)-(2), (b)"
{
  group rehearing-group
  note "Panel rehearing is the ordinary means of reconsideration; rehearing en banc 'is not favored' (Rule 40(a)(1)). A party seeking both must combine them in a single document unless a local rule says otherwise."
  rehearing-panel-considers "Panel (and full court, if en banc sought) considers the petition" -> panel-en-banc-rehearing-decision {
    authority cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(a)(1)-(4)"
  }
}

/// A tribunal-discretion draw. It stays a `decision` by `office`, as in the
/// pack, because a `chance` node lowers to kind `state`; its probabilities
/// are the pack's, with their bases in each edge's note.
chance panel-en-banc-rehearing-decision: "Panel (and, if Combined, the Full Court) Rules on the Petition" by office discretion cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(a)(1)-(4), (c)"
{
  group rehearing-group
  rehearing-denied-edge "Deny rehearing and rehearing en banc" -> rehearing-denied p 0.93 {
    authority cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(a)(1)"
    note "No CAFC-specific published combined grant rate located. Estimate carried over from frap-appellate-procedure.json's panel-rehearing (0.05 grant) and en-banc-poll (0.02 grant) figures, combined and complemented here — 'rehearing en banc is not favored' (Rule 40(a)(1)) and grant rates are exceptionally low across circuits. Flagged APPROXIMATE."
  }
  rehearing-granted-edge "Grant panel rehearing, or grant rehearing en banc" -> rehearing-relief-granted p 0.07 {
    authority cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(e)"
    note "See rehearing-denied-edge's note — same combined-estimate basis, flagged APPROXIMATE."
  }
}

state rehearing-denied: "Rehearing Denied — Panel Decision Stands" by office cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(a)(4)"
{
  group rehearing-group
  rehearing-denied-to-mandate "Mandate clock resumes" -> mandate-issued {
    authority cite "FRAP 41(b); Fed. Cir. R. 41"
    within mandate-period {
      note "Mandate issues 7 days after entry of the order denying a timely petition for panel rehearing and/or rehearing en banc."
    }
  }
}

state rehearing-relief-granted: "Rehearing Granted — Panel Modifies, or Case Reheard En Banc" by office cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(e)"
{
  group rehearing-group
  note "For a granted en banc petition, the panel opinion is vacated and the case is reargued before the full active court; the case is modeled here as looping back into panel-decision to represent the fresh disposition that follows."
  rehearing-granted-to-decision "Case reheard/modified — fresh disposition" -> panel-decision {
    authority cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(e)"
    note "A fresh disposition replaces the prior one, so the panel-outcome flag from the disposition being reheard is cleared here — the new panel-to-affirmed/panel-to-reversed/panel-to-mixed edge that follows sets the flag that matters going forward. Without this, a case that goes through rehearing more than once could accumulate contradictory flags (e.g. panel-affirmed AND panel-reversed at once)."
    clears [panel-affirmed, panel-reversed, panel-mixed]
  }
}

/// Fed. Cir. R. 40(f)(1): a petition for panel rehearing, rehearing en banc,
/// or both is due 30 days after entry of judgment (45 days in a civil case
/// with the United States as a party). FRAP 40(d)(1) sets 14 days "unless
/// the time is shortened or extended by order or local rule"; this rule is
/// that local rule, and an order may still change the time.
rule duty rehearing-petition cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(f)(1)"
{
  deadline rehearing-period: 30.days after Entered(PanelJudgment) counted_by frap26 effective [2025-12-01, ..) known_at 2025-12-01 delegable {
    to CaseOrder
    op set
  } cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(f)(1); FRAP 40(d)(1)"
}

/// FRAP 41(b): the mandate must issue 7 days after entry of an order
/// denying a timely petition for rehearing, and "the court may shorten or
/// extend the time by order". The current text dates from the 2018
/// amendment (Supreme Court order of April 26, 2018, effective December 1,
/// 2018); the 2009 amendment had made the period 7 days, not 7 calendar
/// days, under FRAP 26(a).
rule duty mandate-issuance cite "FRAP 41(b)"
{
  deadline mandate-period: 7.days after Entered(RehearingDenial) counted_by frap26 effective [2018-12-01, ..) known_at 2018-04-26 delegable {
    to CaseOrder
    op set
  } cite "FRAP 41(b)"
}

test "a rehearing petition is due 30 days after entry of judgment" cite "Fed. Cir. R. 40(f)(1)"
{
  given Entered(PanelJudgment) on 2026-03-02
  expect deadline(rehearing-period) == 2026-04-01
}

test "a 30th day on Juneteenth rolls the rehearing petition to Monday" cite "FRAP 26(a)(6)(A)"
{
  given Entered(PanelJudgment) on 2026-05-20
  expect deadline(rehearing-period) == 2026-06-22
}

test "the mandate issues 7 days after rehearing is denied" cite "FRAP 41(b)"
{
  given Entered(RehearingDenial) on 2026-02-27
  expect deadline(mandate-period) == 2026-03-06
}

test "a 7th day on Christmas rolls the mandate to Monday" cite "FRAP 26(a)(6)(A)"
{
  given Entered(RehearingDenial) on 2026-12-18
  expect deadline(mandate-period) == 2026-12-28
}
